Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.24,0:00:08.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was the stone, as red as blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.24,0:00:13.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which promised to turn suffering to delight, bring victory to battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.66,0:00:13.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and life back to the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.25,0:00:19.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In reverence, people referred to it \Nas "The Philosopher's Stone."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.35,0:00:37.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can this be possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.98,0:00:39.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.61,0:00:44.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the answer we finally arrive at \Nafter seeking it for so long?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.45,0:00:49.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can living people be the ingredients for a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.62,0:00:51.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so many of them, to boot!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.16,0:00:57.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.88,0:01:01.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.17,0:01:06.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.89,0:01:12.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.28,0:02:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-Major, p-please, wait a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.41,0:02:51.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.24,0:02:58.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, right now, they appear to be tired, so we probably shouldn't disturb them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.46,0:03:00.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? They're tired?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.71,0:03:04.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll invite them to have dinner,\Nwhich will invigorate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.17,0:03:05.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, no! Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.59,0:03:08.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, the two of them are resting.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.88,0:03:12.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will tell them that\Nyou came by, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.39,0:03:16.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. I guess there's nothing I can do if they're sleeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.96,0:03:45.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,God must really hate people who have committed taboo.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.59,0:03:51.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just when we think things are\Nwithin reach, they run away from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.26,0:03:53.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it repeats.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.89,0:03:59.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And when they're finally within our grasp, we get kicked down by them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.02,0:04:07.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this going to happen\Nfor our whole lives?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.98,0:04:08.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.61,0:04:16.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought that once we found the Philosopher's Stone,\Nour wish would be granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.87,0:04:18.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find it, that's for sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.66,0:04:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, we're trying this hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.04,0:04:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They may say that you're a dog of the military\Nand that you've sold your soul\Nfor special privileges,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.25,0:04:27.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but haven't we persevered without admitting defeat?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.05,0:04:31.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so...\NAnd so, we'll find it for sure, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.03,0:04:56.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.32,0:05:00.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's try starting from square one again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.33,0:05:02.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.50,0:05:06.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a chance that\Nwe misread something.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.71,0:05:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I said I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.75,0:05:11.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what if we try re-reading it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.09,0:05:13.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We might discover something new!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.09,0:05:16.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to give it a shot. Let's keep trying!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.55,0:05:18.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, I've had enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.57,0:05:35.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.53,0:05:38.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.04,0:05:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.54,0:05:50.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't even\Nwant to look at it anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.21,0:05:52.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.47,0:06:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, that's it, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.73,0:06:08.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You won't regret\Nhaving given up here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.86,0:06:17.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is what you've been searching for something you would abandon this easily?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.24,0:06:21.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop going on when you\Ndon't even know the half of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.70,0:06:25.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.08,0:06:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know that you guys are seeking the Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.58,0:06:33.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that it is made by\Nsacrificing living people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.46,0:06:38.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew it was rude,\Nbut I allowed myself to listen in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.09,0:06:41.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've listened in,\Nthen you must know
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.14,0:06:44.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that it won't do any good to investigate any further.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.39,0:06:45.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just leave us alone!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.44,0:06:50.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really are a child, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.81,0:06:55.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're scared, right?\NThat the answers might disappear?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.94,0:07:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't want to acknowledge that everything you've gone through this far
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.65,0:07:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,might be in vain, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.70,0:07:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.80,0:07:18.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't it okay if it doesn't\Nmean anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.59,0:07:27.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Verifying whether or not this means anything is worth something, if you ask me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.77,0:07:31.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you're seeking isn't\Nanything all that simple, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.56,0:07:35.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you keep trying\Na little longer, Edward-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.04,0:07:49.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.83,0:07:53.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though the answers are going to change\Njust because I chuck it\Nall along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.46,0:07:55.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.42,0:07:57.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've come this far!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.88,0:08:00.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can we end it all halfway?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.09,0:08:01.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to\Nsee it to the end!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.43,0:08:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's do it, Al!\NMm-hmm!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.02,0:08:12.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san's research is sound in theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.81,0:08:16.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, it still didn't result in a perfect Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.36,0:08:18.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There still might be other possibilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.44,0:08:19.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.69,0:08:23.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to verify the truth of Marcoh-san's theory with my own eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.45,0:08:25.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.12,0:08:33.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The genuine truth behind truths...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.37,0:08:37.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Behind... truths...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.34,0:08:40.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it! There's something else!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.01,0:08:44.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to this data,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.89,0:08:48.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a considerably large facility would be needed to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.39,0:08:53.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are currently four alchemy laboratories under the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.73,0:08:58.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Among those, Doctor Marcoh was assigned to the 3rd Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.36,0:09:02.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I went around to all of the laboratories in the city,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.61,0:09:05.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there wasn't any research\Nall that remarkable going on there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.86,0:09:07.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.24,0:09:11.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, in the past,\Nthat was the 5th laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.75,0:09:13.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it was closed down,\Nand is deserted now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.50,0:09:17.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a risk of it collapsing, so it was made off-limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.79,0:09:18.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's there!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.80,0:09:20.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.84,0:09:23.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a prison next to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.55,0:09:26.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central 2nd Prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.13,0:09:27.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.43,0:09:29.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With people being the ingredient for a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.06,0:09:34.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what if they did their research there because it was the easiest place to procure them?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.19,0:09:36.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean, they used prisoners?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.15,0:09:37.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.19,0:09:40.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they didn't execute\Ncondemned criminals
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.23,0:09:43.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and instead used them as live materials, that would explain it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.40,0:09:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's in charge of\Nthe laboratories?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.91,0:09:49.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That would have been\NBrig. Gen. Basque Grand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.78,0:09:52.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he was killed by Scar\Nsome time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.96,0:09:57.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.50,0:09:58.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've got no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.42,0:10:01.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How about we check things out directly?\NMm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.80,0:10:03.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,J-Just a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.88,0:10:05.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on,\Nthis is grown-ups' work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.88,0:10:08.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, Scar is still after you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.84,0:10:11.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's too dangerous for you\Nto go walking around outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.14,0:10:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but still...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.76,0:10:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will investigate the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.02,0:10:17.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You wait here, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.52,0:10:19.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we learn anything,\Nwe will report it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.98,0:10:22.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you please...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.48,0:10:25.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.41,0:10:33.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So be it. Okay, it's up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.12,0:10:36.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll ask you to handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.75,0:10:38.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right! Leave it to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.20,0:11:13.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel Hughes,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.74,0:11:18.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm finished writing down the\Ncourt record for case number 3263.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.12,0:11:20.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.62,0:11:22.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, hang on a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.38,0:11:27.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, let's have you continue on with case number 9572, if you would.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.09,0:11:31.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're going to use it in a trial tomorrow, so put a rush on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.26,0:11:33.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.30,0:11:35.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?! Are you tired?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.39,0:11:36.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, not particularly!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.14,0:11:41.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look here! This one is\Na special swimsuit version!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.52,0:11:44.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?\NShe's so cute, it just melts your heart!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.77,0:11:47.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just looking at this, the fatigue just flies away, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.03,0:11:50.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How about it? Hm? Hm?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.36,0:11:53.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.38,0:11:55.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It does, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.31,0:11:56.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.12,0:11:56.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.12,0:11:59.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My daughter is such a little healer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.49,0:11:58.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.37,0:11:59.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the problem there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.83,0:12:01.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, did you find Scar's body?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.33,0:12:04.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not yet, huh?\NAll right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.79,0:12:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As for the matter of us sending security to the library,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.92,0:12:09.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,hurry and take care of that for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.42,0:12:14.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, I've been introduced to quite a find here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.85,0:12:16.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I owe one to Ed for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.91,0:12:37.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tripwire alarms?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.53,0:12:41.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For a building that isn't being used, the security sure is tight, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.41,0:12:42.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is getting more\Nand more suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.04,0:12:44.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, let's go around back.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.09,0:12:52.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.38,0:12:56.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ups-a-daisy!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.06,0:13:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate to say it, \Nbut it's times like this
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.56,0:13:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that I'm glad I don't have my flesh-and-blood arm and leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.48,0:13:07.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Same here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.03,0:13:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This entrance is locked up tight, too, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.66,0:13:18.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, over there...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.17,0:13:28.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like it goes\Nall the way inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.34,0:13:29.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, you wait here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.96,0:13:31.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will you be all right\Nby yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.92,0:13:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right or not, your huge size won't fit through here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.18,0:13:38.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, I'll be back in a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.30,0:13:41.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not this big\Nbecause I wanted to be!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.14,0:13:45.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Lt. Maria Ross.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.94,0:13:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.07,0:13:51.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.44,0:13:53.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, I need to talk to you\Nabout something.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.12,0:14:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.20,0:14:07.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Contact the Command Center at once,\Nand call in reinforcements!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.33,0:14:08.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.47,0:14:18.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no business with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.84,0:14:21.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is Fullmetal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.28,0:14:36.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Two of you stay here!\NWe're going up another stairway!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.53,0:14:38.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's going up to Edward-san's room!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.27,0:15:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So Fullmetal knew about this too?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.00,0:15:29.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't move, Scar!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.21,0:15:38.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.13,0:15:40.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are Edward-san\Nand his brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.01,0:15:42.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.01,0:15:47.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.89,0:15:54.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town of Liore...\Nhas been dealt with\Nall neat and tidy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.07,0:15:58.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no longer anyone there who knows too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.23,0:16:00.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say. Nice work, Envy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.07,0:16:03.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things are going well here too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.62,0:16:06.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal pipsqueak has caught wind of the laboratory, hasn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.37,0:16:11.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we dispose of him \Nbefore it gets out to the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.75,0:16:13.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to kill him,\Nlet me do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.21,0:16:15.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.21,0:16:18.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That boy might just grant us what we want.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.96,0:16:21.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to kill him, it won't be too late to do so after that, will it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.34,0:16:26.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, it's fine with me as long as it doesn't throw a wrench in the works.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.72,0:16:30.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Although, it seems doubtful that\Nhe would ever arrive there safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.93,0:16:38.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told them not to lay a hand on those two, but it is concerning.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.19,0:16:38.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They {\i1}are{\i0} idiots, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.27,0:16:40.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it looks to be too troublesome, dispose of the whole lot of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.07,0:16:42.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.20,0:16:47.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn, this is narrower than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.41,0:16:51.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn it all, if I were normal-sized,\NI wouldn't have gotten through here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.91,0:16:54.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a good thing I'm so little.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.33,0:16:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Augh! No, it's not!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.51,0:17:09.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lights are on...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.68,0:17:12.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So they're not currently using it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.27,0:17:14.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bingo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.99,0:17:24.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What the?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.67,0:17:47.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For them to go this far, they must really not want anyone getting close.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.89,0:17:51.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds interesting!\NI'll take them on!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.92,0:18:26.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey! Aren't we under orders not to lay a hand on them?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.51,0:18:28.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.76,0:18:32.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't rest until I've carved them up!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.43,0:18:35.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait! There are two in our quarry. There are also two of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.64,0:18:38.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't allow you to\Nhave them all to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.23,0:18:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit! This thing is relentless for being just a ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.45,0:19:00.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It really is a good thing\NI'm so small...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.21,0:19:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you! This is a pain!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.36,0:19:27.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on in, they're saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.58,0:19:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice of you to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.75,0:19:44.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I welcome you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.97,0:19:53.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't look very welcoming.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.35,0:19:57.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am he who was entrusted to guard this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.18,0:20:00.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the time being,\Nyou may call me Number 48.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.06,0:20:02.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Number 48?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.73,0:20:06.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been so long. I'm delighted to be able to go against someone so capable.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.61,0:20:08.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have run out of luck\Nby coming up against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.32,0:20:12.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not think ill of me, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.16,0:20:18.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you, don't think ill of me for being the kid who defeated you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.54,0:20:23.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother sure is taking long. What could he be doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.34,0:20:34.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice. You move well for your size.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.72,0:20:35.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's more like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.10,0:20:36.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.01,0:20:39.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should respond when asked who I am, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.52,0:20:42.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My name is Number 66.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.94,0:20:45.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Although, that's just what they call me at work.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.02,0:20:47.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Number 66?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.61,0:20:48.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.69,0:20:52.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do have my own, proper name as well,\Nbut if you heard it, you'd be\Nso surprised you'd wet yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.90,0:20:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll tell you when I finish you off.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.41,0:20:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You say you guard this place, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.66,0:21:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a little something I'd like to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.12,0:21:03.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you can defeat me,\NI will tell you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.87,0:21:05.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.58,0:21:08.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see how good you are!\NYou're fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.01,0:21:12.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your false arm is steel up to\Nthe shoulder, is it? Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.18,0:21:16.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,my beloved sword will pierce even steel!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.64,0:21:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.18,0:21:20.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I bust it again,\NWinry's gonna kill me, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.56,0:21:29.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.57,0:21:34.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oops...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.41,0:21:43.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His reflexes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.96,0:21:45.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.63,0:21:50.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.55,0:21:57.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.14,0:22:03.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.52,0:22:09.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the same kind of\Narmored body as Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.69,0:23:40.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.40,0:23:42.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 20: "Soul of the Guardian"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.78,0:23:47.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've cried a lot, laughed a lot,\Nand seen hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.08,0:23:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These memories are not false.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.29,0:23:52.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am human!
